01:50:44,600 --> 01:50:48,440
So, if the insurance is actually fair, theta is zero.

257
01:50:48,440 --> 01:50:52,680
And in that case, what do people want?

258
01:50:52,680 --> 01:50:53,800
Let's see, well, in that case,

259
01:50:53,800 --> 01:50:56,440
people are going to want amount of insurance

260
01:50:56,440 --> 01:51:01,440
equal to $1,000 over one minus 0.4 X plus 0.4 X.

261
01:51:04,160 --> 01:51:05,880
So, cancels, cancels.

262
01:51:05,880 --> 01:51:09,640
So, this says that when the insurance is actually fair,

263
01:51:09,640 --> 01:51:11,080
then everyone is gonna wanna buy

264
01:51:11,080 --> 01:51:12,660
$1,000 worth of insurance.

265
01:51:14,080 --> 01:51:15,280
All right, and that's interesting,

266
01:51:15,280 --> 01:51:18,880
because the good outcome is $1,000.

267
01:51:18,880 --> 01:51:21,600
Then people also want $1,000 worth of insurance

268
01:51:21,600 --> 01:51:23,600
